 ## Scope
 
-This policy covers the TrustMint contracts, SDK, deployment tooling, and frontend maintained in this repository. Third-party dependency vulnerabilities should be reported to their respective maintainers. Reports about a live deployment should identify the network and contract IDs; do not include private keys, recovery phrases, or personal identity documents.
-
-## Supported code
-
-Security fixes are made against the latest code on `main`. Older tags, forks, and deployed contracts do not update automatically. Contract operators are responsible for assessing and applying upgrades or redeployments.
+This policy covers the six Soroban contract crates under `contracts/`, the TypeScript client library in `sdk/`, the user-facing `frontend/`, and the deployment and development tooling maintained in this repository. Third-party dependency vulnerabilities should be reported to their respective maintainers. Reports about a live deployment should identify the network and contract IDs; do not include private keys, recovery phrases, or personal identity documents.
+
+## Supported versions and branches
+
+The current tagged release is **0.1.0** (see [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md)); changes after that release are tracked under **Unreleased**. Security fixes are maintained on `main` only. We do not backport changes to previous release tags or automatically upgrade deployed contracts.
+
+| Version / branch | Receives security fixes? |
+| --- | --- |
+| `main` (development after `0.1.0`) | Yes — fixes are made on this branch |
+| `0.1.0` (latest tagged release) | No — tag is a frozen snapshot; no backports |
+| Older tags and forks | No — maintainers do not update these automatically |
+
+This describes **repository maintenance policy**, not an assurance that any deployed contract is secure. Contract operators are responsible for independently assessing and applying upgrades or redeployments.
